Report why SE_CRYPTO_Decrypt_Append failed.

DIAGNOSTIC PATCH, off unless -DPORT_SE_CRYPTO_TRACE is passed (SE_PROBE=1
in the Makefile does not enable it; CRYPTO_TRACE=1 does).  It adds two
printf calls and changes no logic.

SE_CRYPTO_Decrypt_Append returns a bare SE_ERROR for a NULL pointer, for a
negative size, and for any mbedTLS failure, and it does not set the
SE_StatusTypeDef, so the caller's trace cannot tell them apart.

The symptom this was written for: ST's installer gets SE_ERROR from the
first SE_Decrypt_Append of the verify pass, while main() makes the same
five calls -- Decrypt_Init, AuthenticateFW_Init, SFU_LL_FLASH_Read,
Decrypt_Append, AuthenticateFW_Append -- against the same image, with the
same chunk size, and every one succeeds.  mbedtls_cipher_update returns
without writing *olen on exactly one path, cipher_info == NULL, and the
observed *olen was unchanged; printing the context pointers says whether
that is what happened or whether the function was not reached at all.

GENERATED WITH diff, NOT BY HAND -- see
patches/0002-sfu_fwimg_no_swap-trace-verify-steps.patch for why.
scratchpad/mkpatch3.py regenerates this file and asserts both anchors
matched.

